From 85b1bbfb6bdbb87a386ea2284c2d9f53dd6a9b22 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PePe Amengual <2208324+jamengual@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 08:10:37 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] kubeadm: build again for Linux, Windows and macOS

The FreeBSD kubeadm commit (WIP: kubeadm on FreeBSD) moved the default
directories into per-OS files but broke every other OS:

- v1beta4/defaults_common.go declared package v1beta3, and both API
  versions declared DefaultCertificatesDir twice; the files were also
  limited to linux || windows. Now !freebsd, deduplicated, right package.
- constants_linux.go held KubernetesDir/KubeletRunDirectory for Linux
  only (macOS had none); it is constants_other.go (!freebsd && !windows).
- The CoreDNS Deployment's capabilities (drop ALL, add NET_BIND_SERVICE)
  were commented out for every OS; they are left out on FreeBSD only.
- The CoreDNS and kube-proxy nodeSelector took runtime.GOOS; it is
  freebsd on FreeBSD and linux elsewhere, as upstream.
- The dns and proxy tests' template data lacked the new OS fields, and
  the constants and dns tests expected Linux paths and manifests on
  FreeBSD. Adds TestCoreDNSDeploymentOS.

kubeadm builds for linux/{arm64,amd64}, windows, darwin and freebsd.
All 55 kubeadm test packages pass on Linux (arm64) except test/cmd's
init tests, which fail identically with stock v1.36.1 kubeadm on a
host that already runs a control plane; the changed packages also pass
on FreeBSD 15.1 and macOS.
